Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.95,0:00:09.01,Default,,0,0,0,,YAMU! YAMU! YAMU! YAMU!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.25,0:00:31.43,Default,,0,0,0,,You're on the move!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.69,0:01:10.81,Default,,0,0,0,,He just summoned the most\Npowerful cards in the game!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.61,0:01:15.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Behold, the three Egyptian gods!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.61,0:01:18.25,Default,,0,0,0,,But I'm not done yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.47,0:01:20.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Next I play Pot of Greed!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.67,0:01:24.99,Default,,0,0,0,,This allows me to take two cards\Nfrom my deck and add them to my hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.25,0:01:29.55,Default,,0,0,0,,How's Yugi gonna get out of this mess?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.01,0:01:30.89,Default,,0,0,0,,There's no way!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.21,0:01:33.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, that dork is\Ndefinitely in over his head.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.35,0:01:35.99,Default,,0,0,0,,I can tell you this much.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.33,0:01:40.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Dueling the Pharaoh is truly the\Nultimate test of Yuki's skills.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.43,0:01:41.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Incredible!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.53,0:01:46.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, since regaining his ancient memories,\Nthe Pharaoh is stronger than ever.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.21,0:01:48.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Joey, what's Yugi gonna do?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.87,0:01:50.01,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't know, Taya.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.21,0:01:53.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Because even though his trap card weakened\NObelisk the Tormentor's attack strength,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.63,0:01:56.15,Default,,0,0,0,,that big fruit still has 2,500 points!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.77,0:02:02.23,Default,,0,0,0,,don't forget about slifer\None lightning blast and
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.31,0:02:05.25,Default,,0,0,0,,yuki's monster takes two\Nthousand points of damage
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.85,0:02:10.01,Default,,0,0,0,,and worst of all if the pharaoh\Nactivates the special ability of the
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.09,0:02:14.57,Default,,0,0,0,,winged dragon of ra he can raise\Nits attack points to almost 15 000
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.89,0:02:21.61,Default,,0,0,0,,this isn't exactly brain surgery\Nhere folks it's pretty obvious
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.69,0:02:25.01,Default,,0,0,0,,that only one of the two yuki\Ntwins inherited the dueling skill,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.09,0:02:26.21,Default,,0,0,0,,so why even watch?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.41,0:02:28.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Looks like his little secret is out.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.85,0:02:31.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi can't duel his\Nway out of a paper bag.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.97,0:02:34.77,Default,,0,0,0,,So he got his look-alike to duel for him.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.93,0:02:38.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Get back here, rich boy.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.05,0:02:42.19,Default,,0,0,0,,This duel ain't over till\Nit's over. Joey's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.47,0:02:44.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, how about showing a little respect?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.15,0:02:49.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you losers honestly believe\Nthat Yugi can still win? You bet!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.67,0:02:51.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Then answer me
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.63,0:02:53.46,Default,,0,0,0,,this.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.54,0:02:57.77,Default,,0,0,0,,What possible combination of cards would\Nyou use to defeat all three Egyptian gods?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.41,0:03:00.47,Default,,0,0,0,,What's your point?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.75,0:03:02.29,Default,,0,0,0,,I rest my case.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.49,0:03:04.37,Default,,0,0,0,,You're as clueless as Yugi is.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.87,0:03:08.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Look, pal, I may not have\Nthe answer, but there is one.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.55,0:03:10.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, Marek, you're the expert here.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.79,0:03:12.08,Default,,0,0,0,,What's their weakness?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.87,0:03:16.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, individually they have drawbacks,\Nbut when all three are together,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.89,0:03:18.01,Default,,0,0,0,,they're practically
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.17,0:03:19.09,Default,,0,0,0,,indestructible.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.17,0:03:21.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Only fate can decide the outcome of this
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.71,0:03:25.01,Default,,0,0,0,,ritual if Yugi is unable\Nto defeat his alter
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.09,0:03:30.37,Default,,0,0,0,,ego then the two are not yet meant to\Nseparate from one another if this occurs the
Dialogue: 0,0:03:30.45,0:03:32.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Pharaoh will be trapped here for another 5
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.79,0:03:37.65,Default,,0,0,0,,,000 years that's not\Nfair I'm so confused I
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.73,0:03:40.43,Default,,0,0,0,,want the Pharaoh to\Nstay but not if it means
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.51,0:03:44.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Trapping him against his\Nwill? Come on, Mokuba.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.35,0:03:51.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Fine. Go, hey, Pharaoh, if you\Nend up having to stick around.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.69,0:03:55.59,Default,,0,0,0,,for a few more years there\Nis a bright side the two of
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.67,0:03:59.05,Default,,0,0,0,,us can finally have that\Nrematch and by the looks of this
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.13,0:04:03.51,Default,,0,0,0,,duel you're not going anywhere\Nthat remains to be seen
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.83,0:04:09.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Kaiba, wait!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.73,0:04:11.81,Default,,0,0,0,,What's the rush?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.01,0:04:15.51,Default,,0,0,0,,I thought you'd love the\Nchance to watch me lose, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.07,0:04:16.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.98,0:04:20.81,Default,,0,0,0,,I only want to see you get\Ncrushed if I'm doing the crushing.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.29,0:04:23.31,Default,,0,0,0,,You owe it to the pharaoh to stay.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.09,0:04:28.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Please take this. My king.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.17,0:04:31.09,Default,,0,0,0,,It is you who is now king.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.53,0:04:36.39,Default,,0,0,0,,You have a bond that goes\Nback thousands of years. And
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.47,0:04:39.65,Default,,0,0,0,,you should be here to say\Ngoodbye to him when he loses
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.25,0:04:42.08,Default,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.19,0:04:45.37,Default,,0,0,0,,You can't be serious.\NMore serious than I've
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.45,0:04:48.71,Default,,0,0,0,,ever been in my life\NThose Egyptian gods may be
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.79,0:04:51.77,Default,,0,0,0,,strong But they're not\Nundefeatable And I'm
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.85,0:04:57.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Gonna take them down one by\None. You're nuts. Wow, cool.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.77,0:05:02.59,Default,,0,0,0,,now if you don't mind\Ni have myself a duel to
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.67,0:05:08.11,Default,,0,0,0,,win i'm proud of you yugi\Nwell done come on you
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.19,0:05:10.97,Default,,0,0,0,,mean to tell me you\Nactually have a strategy in
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.05,0:05:14.07,Default,,0,0,0,,mind for defeating all\Nthree egyptian god cards
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.53,0:05:22.23,Default,,0,0,0,,fine then this i gotta see and when\Nyou fail miserably i'll step in and
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.31,0:05:24.31,Default,,0,0,0,,show you what real dueling's all about
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.39,0:05:29.73,Default,,0,0,0,,All right. Ready Yugi? Ready Pharaoh?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.59,0:05:43.93,Default,,0,0,0,,it won't be easy but i need to\Ndefeat all three egyptian god cards
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.19,0:05:53.97,Default,,0,0,0,,it's the only way for me to pass\Nthis test and free the pharaoh
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.05,0:05:58.51,Default,,0,0,0,,by proving that i'm ready to be\Non my own ever since our spirits
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.59,0:06:02.65,Default,,0,0,0,,joined together i've always let the\Npharaoh take the lead during our
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.73,0:06:07.99,Default,,0,0,0,,duels but every obstacle we faced\Ntogether pushed me to try harder
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.65,0:06:12.77,Default,,0,0,0,,And I always knew that someday I'd\Nbe good enough to walk by his side.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.09,0:06:14.95,Default,,0,0,0,,I just hope that day's today.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.59,0:06:16.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.57,0:06:20.97,Default,,0,0,0,,I can see the uncertainty in your eyes,\Nand if you expect to win this duel,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.05,0:06:24.09,Default,,0,0,0,,you must first overcome\Nyour self-doubt. Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.63,0:06:27.17,Default,,0,0,0,,I believe that's why\Nfate brought us together,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.25,0:06:29.77,Default,,0,0,0,,so that you could learn\Nto trust in yourself
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.85,0:06:32.89,Default,,0,0,0,,and be the duelist that\Nyou truly are inside.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.35,0:06:36.25,Default,,0,0,0,,And so that I could learn from you. Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.99,0:06:38.83,Default,,0,0,0,,You know what?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.05,0:06:41.82,Default,,0,0,0,,What the Pharaoh's saying\Nmakes a lot of sense.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.03,0:06:44.41,Default,,0,0,0,,I wouldn't be who I am without you.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.71,0:06:49.30,Default,,0,0,0,,And I thought about everything that you\Ntaught me when I was building my deck.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.51,0:06:52.10,Default,,0,0,0,,That's exactly what I\Ndid when I built mine.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.39,0:06:55.59,Default,,0,0,0,,You taught me about\Nbravery and about having
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.67,0:06:58.39,Default,,0,0,0,,self-confidence even\Nwhen all hope seems lost.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.59,0:07:01.65,Default,,0,0,0,,And I thought about that with\Nevery card that I picked.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.73,0:07:06.35,Default,,0,0,0,,And you taught me about friendship\Nand having compassion for others.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.33,0:07:08.37,Default,,0,0,0,,In Duelist Kingdom,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.45,0:07:11.71,Default,,0,0,0,,you showed me that there are some\Nthings more important than winning.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.79,0:07:13.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Like the safety of a friend.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.59,0:07:19.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Each of us has given the other a gift.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:19.39,0:07:20.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Like bravery.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.89,0:07:23.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, and kindness, sympathy, and heart.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.13,0:07:24.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Wow.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.15,0:07:27.50,Default,,0,0,0,,So even though our minds have separated,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.61,0:07:30.23,Default,,0,0,0,,each of us has maintained\Nthe other one's strengths.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.31,0:07:33.19,Default,,0,0,0,,And those strengths are\Nrepresented in our decks.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.39,0:07:38.81,Default,,0,0,0,,So we're pretty evenly\Nmatched. That's right. That
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.89,0:07:41.87,Default,,0,0,0,,was just the kind of pep\Ntalk i needed i have to
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.95,0:07:44.13,Default,,0,0,0,,admit part of me was\Nworried that the sides of
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.21,0:07:47.47,Default,,0,0,0,,this duel were uneven but\Nnow i realize that even
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.55,0:07:50.61,Default,,0,0,0,,though the pharaoh has all\Nthree egyptian god cards
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.69,0:07:54.41,Default,,0,0,0,,i have everything i need\Nto stop them and that's
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.49,0:07:58.75,Default,,0,0,0,,exactly what i'm gonna\Ndo pharaoh i believe it's
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.83,0:08:03.07,Default,,0,0,0,,My move. That's right. Now\Ngo. Don't mind if I do.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.83,0:08:04.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Sweet. Nice.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.21,0:08:06.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Do your grunts proud, Yuki.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.25,0:08:09.43,Default,,0,0,0,,First of all, since it's my turn again,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.51,0:08:14.57,Default,,0,0,0,,my swordsman moves up in the world,\Nadvancing from level three to level four.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.75,0:08:17.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Cool.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.66,0:08:19.91,Default,,0,0,0,,That bad boy's got 3,000 points now.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.09,0:08:21.97,Default,,0,0,0,,That's enough to defeat Obelisk.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.35,0:08:25.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Next, I'll send my three\NMagnet Warriors, Alpha,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:25.53,0:08:27.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Beta, and Gamma, straight to my graveyard.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.93,0:08:32.81,Default,,0,0,0,,That lets me summon my Valkyra\Nthe Magna Warrior in attack mode!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.63,0:08:37.41,Default,,0,0,0,,You've just activated Slifer the\NSky Dragon's special ability,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.81,0:08:40.69,Default,,0,0,0,,which means that your\NMagna Warrior is weakened!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.73,0:08:50.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Not quite, cause I have a backup plan!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.83,0:08:54.03,Default,,0,0,0,,So now I activate the\NMagic Card Mirage spell!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.41,0:09:08.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Mirage Spell is activated when\None of my monsters is targeted.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.61,0:09:13.19,Default,,0,0,0,,It negates Slifer's blast and\Nincreases my life points by 2,000!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.39,0:09:17.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.39,0:09:18.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Way to play, Yugi!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.11,0:09:21.52,Default,,0,0,0,,You gotta admit, that was pretty awesome.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.71,0:09:26.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Using Slifer's ability to restore his\Nlife points may have been a decent move.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.85,0:09:30.97,Default,,0,0,0,,But it's going to take a lot more than\Nthat to defeat the three Egyptian gods.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.05,0:09:33.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Next I place two cards\Nface down on the field.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.63,0:09:35.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Your move, Pharaoh.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.61,0:09:43.49,Default,,0,0,0,,That's strange.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.71,0:09:45.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Why didn't Yugi just attack Obelisk?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.99,0:09:47.99,Default,,0,0,0,,I guess he didn't want to take the risk.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.07,0:09:51.59,Default,,0,0,0,,A careless attack on an Egyptian\Ngod could easily backfire.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.85,0:09:54.49,Default,,0,0,0,,But there's still one\Nthing that I don't get.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.57,0:09:58.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Why did Yugi leave all his monsters\Non the field in attack mode?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.07,0:10:02.54,Default,,0,0,0,,It's not like Yugi to leave\Nhimself wide open to an attack.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.81,0:10:06.05,Default,,0,0,0,,If you have a strategy,\Nthen let's see you use it.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.97,0:10:09.50,Default,,0,0,0,,What could he be planning?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.77,0:10:12.30,Default,,0,0,0,,For some reason, he\Nmust want me to attack.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.79,0:10:15.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Otherwise, he wouldn't have left\Nhis monsters in attack mode.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.03,0:10:20.01,Default,,0,0,0,,They may be powerful, but they're\Nno match for my Egyptian gods.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.57,0:10:23.11,Default,,0,0,0,,I guess there's only one way to find out.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.71,0:10:25.95,Default,,0,0,0,,My move. I draw.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.41,0:10:28.03,Default,,0,0,0,,And you know what that means.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.11,0:10:33.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Since I'm now holding four cards,\NSlyfer's attack points increased to 4,000.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.29,0:10:35.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, Slifer, attack!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.37,0:10:40.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Destroy his swordsman\Nwith Thunder Force Strike!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.85,0:10:42.87,Default,,0,0,0,,You just triggered my trap!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:43.87,0:10:46.97,Default,,0,0,0,,But Yugi, trap cards\Ndon't work against Slifer.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.57,0:10:55.67,Default,,0,0,0,,It's just too strong. Of course\NI've been saying that all along.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.09,0:11:16.35,Default,,0,0,0,,This is not looking hopeful, Yugi. This\Nwould be a good time for that strategy.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.89,0:11:20.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Winged Dragon of Ra,\Nattack his Magna Warrior!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.07,0:11:30.21,Default,,0,0,0,,There goes monster number two!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.97,0:11:39.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks to Sniper and Ra,\NYugi's out of monsters now.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.51,0:11:43.03,Default,,0,0,0,,And the Pharaoh can still attack\Nwith his last Egyptian god.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.11,0:11:45.83,Default,,0,0,0,,One shot from Obelisk and Yugi's a goner.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.35,0:11:47.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.25,0:11:50.15,Default,,0,0,0,,It's done?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.55,0:11:52.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, like you're surprised?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.77,0:11:56.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi, I know you tried your best.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.35,0:11:58.09,Default,,0,0,0,,For that, I am forever thankful.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.17,0:12:01.55,Default,,0,0,0,,But now, the time has come\Nfor me to end this duel.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.29,0:12:06.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Obelisk, wipe out his life\Npoints with your fist of fate!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.03,0:12:12.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, no! Yugi!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.55,0:12:15.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Valkyra!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.01,0:12:17.91,Default,,0,0,0,,But how?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.37,0:12:20.11,Default,,0,0,0,,This doesn't make any sense.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.43,0:12:27.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi, I already sent those\Nmonsters to the graveyard.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.11,0:12:31.11,Default,,0,0,0,,How were you able to\Nbring them back? Easy.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.53,0:12:33.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Remember the last trap card I played?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.61,0:12:37.59,Default,,0,0,0,,His life points just came back.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.81,0:12:40.16,Default,,0,0,0,,I knew Yugi had something up his sleeve.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.35,0:12:44.21,Default,,0,0,0,,My Mirage Ruler trap card automatically\Nactivates whenever all of the
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.29,0:12:49.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Monsters on my side of the field are\Ndestroyed by my opponent in one turn. It
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.17,0:12:52.63,Default,,0,0,0,,brings my monsters back to the field\Nand restores my life points to the
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.71,0:12:57.61,Default,,0,0,0,,number i had before your turn began\Nplus it only cost me a thousand points
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.75,0:13:03.93,Default,,0,0,0,,well done i'm impressed\Nnow obelisk can't destroy
Dialogue: 0,0:13:04.01,0:13:06.87,Default,,0,0,0,,yuki's life points looks\Nlike he saved himself
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.45,0:13:11.41,Default,,0,0,0,,for now i have no choice\Nbut to end my turn now
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.25,0:13:16.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Dude, that was too close for\Ncomfort. How about you? You
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.07,0:13:21.05,Default,,0,0,0,,hanging in there gramps so\Nfar so good but my kicker
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.13,0:13:24.69,Default,,0,0,0,,can't take much more of\Nthis ah come on i've seen
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.77,0:13:27.35,Default,,0,0,0,,you duel and you're stronger\Nthan any of us come to
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.43,0:13:29.79,Default,,0,0,0,,think of it i do keep\Nmyself in pretty good shape
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.87,0:13:33.15,Default,,0,0,0,,don't die who do you think\Nmr king of games inherited
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.23,0:13:39.39,Default,,0,0,0,,his strength from yuki i've\Nnever been more proud of
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.47,0:13:45.71,Default,,0,0,0,,You than I am today. Thank\Ngoodness. When did I start
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.79,0:13:50.93,Default,,0,0,0,,rooting for yuki hey bro it\Nlooks like yuki's holding
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.01,0:13:54.07,Default,,0,0,0,,his own against those\Negyptian gods please the only
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.15,0:13:56.59,Default,,0,0,0,,thing that geek did was\Nstall for a little more time
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.67,0:13:59.37,Default,,0,0,0,,in order for him to win\Nhe needs to figure out the
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.45,0:14:02.67,Default,,0,0,0,,weakness of each egyptian\Ngod card so what are their
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.75,0:14:06.15,Default,,0,0,0,,weaknesses that's something\Nthat even i'm not sure of
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.23,0:14:10.27,Default,,0,0,0,,but i know they exist The\Nfirst major weakness is that
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.35,0:14:13.33,Default,,0,0,0,,three sacrifices are required\Nin order to summon them.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:13.41,0:14:17.41,Default,,0,0,0,,But since they're already on the\Nfield, that weakness was eliminated.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.49,0:14:19.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Now it's up to Yugi to do the impossible.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.27,0:14:23.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Find the fatal flaws of the most\Npowerful monsters in the game.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.29,0:14:29.65,Default,,0,0,0,,There's no way Yugi can win this duel.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.93,0:14:32.11,Default,,0,0,0,,He's not even the true king of games.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.37,0:14:36.91,Default,,0,0,0,,All this time, someone else has been\Ndueling for him while he took the credit.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.99,0:14:41.87,Default,,0,0,0,,I feel as if Yugi is going to turn\Nthings around in his next move. Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.13,0:14:43.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Have you seen the future?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.79,0:14:46.50,Default,,0,0,0,,I haven't had a vision\Nof the future in years.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.91,0:14:49.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's just call this a strong hunch.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.23,0:14:52.58,Default,,0,0,0,,So you think Yugi has a chance\Nagainst the Egyptian gods?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.69,0:14:53.87,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm not sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.25,0:14:58.51,Default,,0,0,0,,But something just occurred to me that\Nperhaps I hadn't thought about before.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.59,0:15:01.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe fate chose Yugi as\Nthe vessel for the pharaoh's
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.81,0:15:04.57,Default,,0,0,0,,spirit not because he\Nneeded the pharaoh's help,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.65,0:15:08.31,Default,,0,0,0,,But because Yugi himself is the\Nmodern-day version of the pharaoh,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.39,0:15:09.51,Default,,0,0,0,,equal in every way.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.89,0:15:11.77,Default,,0,0,0,,The two were brought together because they
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.85,0:15:14.49,Default,,0,0,0,,represent opposite sides of the same soul.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.33,0:15:16.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, but they're so...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.41,0:15:17.24,Default,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.32,0:15:19.00,Default,,0,0,0,,They're so different\Nfrom one another because
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.09,0:15:22.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi's shy and the pharaoh's\Nassertive and confident?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.27,0:15:25.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, the truth is they each had\Na quality that the other needed,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.71,0:15:28.39,Default,,0,0,0,,so they learned from each other. Hold on.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:28.81,0:15:31.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you saying they're complete now?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.11,0:15:33.05,Default,,0,0,0,,We'll soon find out.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.29,0:15:35.64,Default,,0,0,0,,If their journey together is truly over,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.75,0:15:40.71,Default,,0,0,0,,then fate will allow Yugi to defeat all\Nthree Egyptian god cards and win the duel.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.81,0:15:46.69,Default,,0,0,0,,All right.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.97,0:15:50.67,Default,,0,0,0,,If I expect to win this, I need to\Nstart thinking like the Pharaoh.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.75,0:15:54.49,Default,,0,0,0,,For starters, I need to figure\Nout what his face down card is.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.67,0:15:57.37,Default,,0,0,0,,For some reason, he\Nhasn't activated it yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.09,0:16:02.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait, come to think of it, I haven't launched\None attack since he played that card.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.97,0:16:06.41,Default,,0,0,0,,I bet he's planning to use it to\Nmake one of my attacks backfire.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.49,0:16:08.17,Default,,0,0,0,,So it must be Mirror Force.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.47,0:16:12.94,Default,,0,0,0,,If I'm right, then there might be a way\NI can take down those Egyptian gods.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.27,0:16:15.13,Default,,0,0,0,,But it's not going to be easy.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.49,0:16:18.13,Default,,0,0,0,,I need to play the right card combination.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.35,0:16:21.29,Default,,0,0,0,,So everything is riding on this next draw.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:21.89,0:16:24.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, heart of the\Ncards, you know the deal.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.87,0:16:25.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Guide me.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.17,0:16:28.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Alright, now!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.61,0:16:30.99,Default,,0,0,0,,My move, and I have a plan!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.35,0:16:32.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Good, then go!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.83,0:16:34.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi's not gonna attack, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.31,0:16:36.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Nah!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.22,0:16:41.53,Default,,0,0,0,,For starters, my Silent Swordsman jumps\None more notch from level 4 to level 5!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:43.71,0:16:48.27,Default,,0,0,0,,And then I'll activate Valkyra,\Nthe Magna Warrior's special effect!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.75,0:16:50.16,Default,,0,0,0,,You see, whenever Alpha,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.35,0:16:54.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Beta, and Gamma, the Magnet Warriors,\Nare in my graveyard at the same time,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.75,0:16:59.43,Default,,0,0,0,,I can bring them all back to the\Nfield by sacrificing my Valkyra!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.19,0:17:02.03,Default,,0,0,0,,He's completely lost it.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.41,0:17:05.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Why on earth would Yugi dismantle\None of his most powerful
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.75,0:17:09.52,Default,,0,0,0,,monsters just to summon three\Nweaker monsters to take its place?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.67,0:17:23.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Whenever you summon a new monster,\NSlifer's special ability activates.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.75,0:17:27.77,Default,,0,0,0,,What are you thinking, Yugi?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:28.01,0:17:31.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Now every one of your monsters\Ngets blown off the field.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.11,0:17:34.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Lightning blast!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.21,0:17:38.95,Default,,0,0,0,,So far, so good.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.27,0:17:41.79,Default,,0,0,0,,I activate my Magnet Force trap!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:45.73,0:17:46.69,Default,,0,0,0,,What's this?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.99,0:17:50.87,Default,,0,0,0,,I can activate Magnet Force\Nwhenever one of my rock-or-machine
Dialogue: 0,0:17:50.95,0:17:54.66,Default,,0,0,0,,monsters is targeted by the\Nspecial ability of another monster.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.03,0:17:59.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Once activated, this trap card transfers\NSlifer's Blast to your monsters.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.83,0:18:02.91,Default,,0,0,0,,He's turning the Egyptian\Ngods against themselves.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.59,0:18:06.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Is this move really gonna work?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.29,0:18:18.93,Default,,0,0,0,,He weakened them by 2,000 points.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.01,0:18:23.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Now Yuge Swordsman can take on any\None of those Egyptian god-gods!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.71,0:18:26.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Silent Swordsman, it's time to attack!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:26.65,0:18:30.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Destroy Obelisk the Tormentor\Nwith Silent Sword Slash!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.11,0:18:33.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Not so fast, Yuge!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.27,0:18:35.89,Default,,0,0,0,,I activate my trap card!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.53,0:18:38.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Behold, my Mirror Force!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.09,0:18:40.07,Default,,0,0,0,,No way!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.33,0:18:54.61,Default,,0,0,0,,It's over, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.37,0:18:57.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Aw, man.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.71,0:18:59.33,Default,,0,0,0,,All his monsters are gone.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.85,0:19:02.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Dude, this can't be happening. Yugi!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:02.93,0:19:05.45,Default,,0,0,0,,He came closer than I thought possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.39,0:19:07.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:07.30,0:19:11.93,Default,,0,0,0,,well, close doesn't count, so in my book,\NYugi's still the same loser he always was.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:12.51,0:19:13.51,Default,,0,0,0,,What a joke.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:13.87,0:19:16.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Once again, you've all wasted my time.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.55,0:19:18.13,Default,,0,0,0,,That was a valiant effort, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:18.21,0:19:21.17,Default,,0,0,0,,If only you had predicted\Nmy face down card.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:21.53,0:19:24.69,Default,,0,0,0,,I did, and that's why\Nthis duel's not done!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.01,0:19:28.11,Default,,0,0,0,,As soon as your Mirror Force\NTrap card was activated,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.19,0:19:31.60,Default,,0,0,0,,I was able to complete the\Ncard combination that I needed!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.07,0:19:37.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Pharaoh, it's about time I eliminated\Nthose Egyptian God cards! But how?
